INT. OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - FOURTH FLOOR - DAY

Cubicles. Beige. A ficus dying with dignity.

PRIYANKA, thirties, presses a stapler into the carpet. WENDELL, fifties, stares at an empty slide. LUCIA, twenties, hides behind a monitor. HAROLD, sixties, sleeps upright. A TALL MAN, forties, stands unannounced at the end of the aisle, a clipboard under his arm.

PRIYANKA
Who is that?

WENDELL
(shrugging)
Consultant.

The Tall Man walks to Wendell's desk. He places his clipboard down. Wendell does not look up. Lucia slides lower.

TALL MAN
Efficiency review.

WENDELL
Of course.

PHONE (V.O.)
(from Wendell's desk)
Wendell, this is the CEO. Is the review underway?

WENDELL
(into the phone, calm)
It's underway, sir.

The Tall Man takes out a pen. Harold snores. Priyanka drops the stapler and it echoes. Lucia peeks over the edge of her monitor and meets the Tall Man's eyes.

MR. GRAVES
(to Lucia)
You. Name?

LUCIA
Lucia.

MR. GRAVES
Redundant.

Lucia stands. She picks up her coat. Priyanka rises, Wendell rises, Harold wakes with a start, and all four stare as Mr. Graves strikes off a line on his clipboard.
